WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.261
- I'm back with our Ready to Rock hour.

00:00:03.261 --> 00:00:05.382
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:07.150
(laughter)

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:07.983
Okay.

00:00:07.983 --> 00:00:10.140
We've got legendary drummer Sheila E,

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.570
sitting in with the band y'all.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.436
Give it up!

00:00:12.436 --> 00:00:13.478
(applause)

00:00:13.478 --> 00:00:14.870
Yes.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.880
My next guest is another
legendary woman of rock.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.270
She's won two Grammys,

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.450
and an Academy Award for her music.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.390
During the pandemic,

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.440
she created a concert streaming service,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.740
to bring live music to all of us at home.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.460
It's called Etheridge TV.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.958
Give it up for Melissa Etheridge! (claps)

00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:35.143
(upbeat rock music)
(applause)

00:00:35.143 --> 00:00:36.206
- Hi there.

00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:37.039
- What's up.

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:38.300
I love your rock and roll room.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.102
Your whole vibe right now.

00:00:40.102 --> 00:00:40.935
(laughter)

00:00:40.935 --> 00:00:41.768
- That's what we're doing.

00:00:41.768 --> 00:00:43.350
This is Etheridge TV.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.700
My wife and I put this together.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.180
We're in our garage.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.110
We call ourselves two moms in a garage.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.970
And we, you know, put it all together,

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.440
during kind of a healing
time that we needed.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.110
And this is our vibe.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.548
- Dude, your garage is way
cooler than mine. (laughs)

00:00:59.548 --> 00:01:00.381
(laughter)

00:01:00.381 --> 00:01:01.214
(laughs) I'm like, I need,

00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:03.372
I have like, garage
envy right now. (laughs)

00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:04.205
(laughter)

00:01:04.205 --> 00:01:06.048
I have like a Christmas
tree and some boxes.

00:01:06.048 --> 00:01:07.500
(laughs) I was like,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.900
So, I actually sang, "I'm The Only One"

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.680
for one of our karaokes last year.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.940
I love singing your music,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.980
because I get to just wail.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.810
It's just such a freeing thing.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.080
Listen, do you know Sheila E?

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.420
She's actually sitting in with us today.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.647
Y'all know each other?
- I do. Sheila, wow!

00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:25.000
- Hi Melissa!

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:25.987
I miss you!

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:28.312
- I miss you!

00:01:28.312 --> 00:01:29.690
We need to rock soon.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:30.523
Come on!

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.370
- I know. Let's go!

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.240
I'm coming over.
(laughter)

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.130
- Like this connection.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.130
In weird COVID times, over screens.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.234
I like it.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.830
(laughter)

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.940
So, well, today is
dedicated to rock and roll.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:43.610
And we've asked Jon Bon Jovi earlier,

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.060
what defines rock music for you?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.010
- Well to me, rock and
roll has always been,

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:52.760
the music that we aren't
supposed to listen to as youth.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.853
You know, it was,

00:01:55.076 --> 00:01:57.610
it started with being, you know,

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.300
it's very sexual in nature.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.720
It's about the taboos,

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.670
and it's about breaking the social norms.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:05.710
And it's,

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:10.710
if you watch how rock and roll
sort of changed over time,

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.790
and we sort of changed over time.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.540
Now, I consider your hip hop and rap,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.850
sort of rock and roll now,

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.360
because it's the music that

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.646
you don't want your kids to
listen to, you know. (laughs)

00:02:20.646 --> 00:02:22.232
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:02:22.232 --> 00:02:23.065
So you,

00:02:23.065 --> 00:02:23.898
you're such a mom.

00:02:23.898 --> 00:02:26.600
So who were your musical
inspirations growing up?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.880
Who were people you weren't
supposed to listen to,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.850
and you wanted to become. (laughs)

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.000
- Right. (laughs)

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.330
Well, Bruce Springsteen.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.280
You know, Bruce Springsteen was,

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.320
he just seemed to have the answers for me,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.300
as far as rock and roll,
you know, was going.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.720
I probably ended up somewhere between

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.900
Janis Joplin and Bruce
Springsteen, you know. (laughs)

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:42.733
- Oh my God.

00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:43.566
I remember that time,

00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:44.399
I think it was on the Grammys,

00:02:44.399 --> 00:02:46.140
and you covered "Piece of My Heart"

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.720
Holy moly.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.770
I was like,

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.917
so, I kind of wanted to quit.

00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:52.523
(laughs) 'Cause I was like, well,

00:02:52.523 --> 00:02:53.356
(laughter)

00:02:53.356 --> 00:02:54.360
never gonna do anything like that.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.193
Like, it was just,

00:02:55.193 --> 00:02:56.353
it was amazing.

00:02:57.493 --> 00:02:58.480
And it just was one of those times,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.650
I feel like when,

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.110
we all love singing,
we all are performing,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.250
but there's times when like,

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.520
you don't even remember what happened,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.353
and you become the vessel

00:03:04.353 --> 00:03:05.850
for something so much
bigger than yourself.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.710
And that just felt like
that to me watching it.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.470
- It was a very healing moment for me.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.440
I was bald from chemotherapy.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.570
I had to,

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.380
I had gone through that,

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.740
and it was my first time on stage,

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.170
or even in front of people.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.340
I hadn't even been in crowds.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.180
I was still doing radiation treatments.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.410
And it meant a lot to me to get up.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.863
And it was a big changing
moment in my life.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.440
I, it's kind of before
that Grammys and after,

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.240
is kind of my musical career. (laughs)

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.073
- Yeah.

00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:36.742
- And, yeah that was it.

00:03:36.742 --> 00:03:39.700
That was one of my top
five moments ever. (laughs)

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.533
- Oh my God.

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:41.366
Well, that's so funny,

00:03:41.366 --> 00:03:42.620
'cause literally we have
shared the stage before,

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.200
and I was freaking out.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.870
Putting my best Meryl Streep on,

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.520
acting like I was like, totally fine.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.730
- Yeah, oh it's so sweet.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.979
And it's very important to me,

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:54.960
as I've gone through this, my career,

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.710
to really reach out to the
women who are coming up,

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.100
and making a name.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.830
And you were just hitting your stride.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.160
You were really doing great.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:04.993
And you know,

00:04:04.993 --> 00:04:09.060
you also, hold that sort
of rock and roll torch,

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.510
but also you are just
a down to earth person.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.420
- Oh, thank you.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.730
That means a lot coming from you.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.750
I know,

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.260
I mean, it's been a difficult
year for me personally.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.390
It's been a difficult
year for a lot of people.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.180
And I know as well for you.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.710
So how do you get there?

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.420
Does music help you?

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:26.790
- Absolutely.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:31.180
The moment I realized we
were going into lockdown,

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.260
that's when I started
these concerts from home.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.110
And I started them,

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.070
first, we were just in
our office back there,

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.430
with like one little camera,

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:40.070
one, not, you know, my phone,

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.960
and going on Facebook.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.240
Do that every day.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.820
And I would have gone longer,

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.510
but my son passed away.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.080
Lost him to opioid addiction in may.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.380
And that was when I,

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.390
my wife and I decided
we're gonna come out here,

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.720
to our garage.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.440
We're going to build a
studio that we can stream in,

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.900
like a real studio.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.210
And we created Etheridge TV,

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.550
where three nights a week,

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.950
Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays,

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.300
I do music.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.570
I just finished a show,

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.193
a cover show about
Stevie wonder, you know.

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:14.100
And so,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.751
and it's a subscription service.

00:05:15.751 --> 00:05:16.650
You go, Melissa,

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.110
Etheridge TV,

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.480
etheridgetv.com

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.130
subscribe, 50 bucks a month,

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:24.409
and you get 25 shows or what I, yeah.

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:26.479
25 shows, that's it.
- Wow!

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:27.312
That's a lot!

00:05:28.297 --> 00:05:29.210
- Yeah, yeah.
- Like, you're working hard.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.704
That's a lot of work.

00:05:30.704 --> 00:05:31.680
(laughter)

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.200
- Absolutely. You know what?

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.460
It keeps me sane, it
keeps me out of trouble,

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.440
and I'm playing music, and
I'm actually getting better.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.180
I've got, you know, guitars and pianos,

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.020
and everything in here, and I'm just--

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.680
- I love that you just
said, you're getting better.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.044
And you are a legend. (laughs)

00:05:43.044 --> 00:05:44.540
(laughter)

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.020
I'm getting better. (laughs)

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:47.970
- It's important.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.430
It's important to keep learning.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.434
- Yes, of course.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:51.547
- And I learned all about streaming,

00:05:51.547 --> 00:05:53.740
and cameras and everything.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.960
- No, of course, of course.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.500
Well, we have a young girl,

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.030
aspiring to achieve everything you have.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.800
She is remarkable.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.740
I mean, she's super talented.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.393
So, I was wondering will
you help us surprise her?

00:06:06.443 --> 00:06:07.570
- Absolutely.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.980
- Okay, awesome, awesome. Okay.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.010
Well, we're gonna take
you off Skype for a bit,

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.650
so she doesn't know you're here,

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:14.080
then we're gonna bring you back,

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.540
right at the right moment, alright?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.040
- Got you. I'll be right here.

